## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop:** `st` object from `newGame()`; `R(st)` mulberry32 stream used everywhere (genMap, addColonist, events); `endTurn()` calls stepStorm→stepPower→stepProduction→stepNeeds→stepMorale→stepPopulation→stepCaravan→stepEvents→stepEndCheck in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map:** 8x8 (`W=8`,`NT=64`); `genMap` uses seeded `R(st)`; `canBuildAt` checks `b.ter.includes(t.tr)`; `adjMult` multiplies `m` in `prodBreakdown`, changing `out.outs`. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy:** water→soil→food and ore→metal chains (`soilworks`,`greenhouse`,`mine`,`forge`); `caps()` enforced in `addRes`, overflow logged and tracked in `stats.overflow`. Score 2.

**F4 — Population:** colonist records with `skill,fatigue,morale,job,assigned`; `skillMult`/fatigue thresholds read inside `prodBreakdown`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs:** `stepNeeds` consumes food/water, sets `shortNow`; `stepMorale` applies `dm-=12` per shortage; `moraleMult` feeds back into production; +3/turn recovery when fed. Score 2.

**F6 — Research:** 10 nodes in `RESEARCH`; `researchStatus` enforces `r.req`; `payCost` deducts; every id (filtration/hydroponics/smelting/geotaps/masonry/shelters/logistics/radio/messhall/machining) has a real read site (`resMult`, `damageBld`, `unlockedBld`, `caps`). Score 2.

**F7 — Events:** 12 entries in `EVENTS`; weighted pick via `tw`/`roll` in `stepEvents`; 6 events (refugees,bloom,pedlar,sickness,vault,strike) have 2-3 differing choices; `evCd[ev.id]=8` cooldown decremented each turn. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade:** `priceOf` reads `st.res[r]`/cap scarcity and `cv.drift[r]` (random-walked every turn); `cv.inv` limits `tradeBuy`; both `tradeBuy`/`tradeSell` wired to `ui.buy`/`ui.sell`. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard:** `stormDue` every 8 turns; `stormSeverity` grows with `turn`; `prodBreakdown` cuts output ×0.6 at hp<70, disables at hp<30; `shelters` research and `stormwall` building reduce `damageBld` amount; `repair` costs parts + colonist fatigue. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load:** `serialize(st)` → textarea for manual copy; `loadState`→`validateState` throws descriptive errors shown via `UI.saveErr`. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions:** win (`turn===60 && cols.length>=12 && needsMet`) and lose (`cols.length<=0`) both in `stepEndCheck`; `scoreOf` combines pop/research/stock/turns; modal summary in `maybeModals`. Score 2.

**F12 — UI:** `ui.tab` switches panels; `log()` stores `t:st.turn`, rendered `T${l.t}`; extensive `data-tip` tooltips explaining formulas; keydown handles Space/Digit1-6; `@media(max-width:520px)` layout. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel:** `runTests()` asserts real invariants (cap respect, prereq enforcement, save/load hash roundtrip, storm/repair economics); `runBenchmark` runs `simulate()` 200 turns headlessly via `policyTurn`, prints `stateHash`. Score 2.

**G1:** `resMult` reads `st.done` (filtration/hydroponics/smelting), multiplied into `m` in `prodBreakdown`, applied to `out.outs`; geotaps is a hardcoded +2 add in `stepProduction` (minor special case). Score 4.

**G2:** `stepNeeds` sets `shortNow`→`stepMorale` applies `dm-=12`→`c.morale`→`moraleMult(w)` read in `prodBreakdown` next turn's output. Score 4.

**G3:** `stepStorm`→`damageBld` reduces `t.b.hp`→`prodBreakdown` cuts/disables output by hp→`repair` spends parts+labor→hp restored to 100, output resumes. Score 4.

**G4:** `priceOf` = `BASEP*drift[r]*scarcity(st.res[r]/cap)`; `drift` random-walked every turn in `stepCaravan`; feeds `buyPrice`/`sellPrice`. Score 4.

**G5:** refugees choices: `addColonist`+`subRes` vs `bumpMorale`; sickness choices: `c.fatigue=100` set directly vs `subRes` food/water — both durable state writes beyond log. Score 4.

